<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="60589" href="schedule/2014/spring/GLBL/296/60589.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2014" href="schedule/2014.xml">2014</calendarYear><term id="120141" href="schedule/2014/spring.xml">Spring 2014</term><subject id="GLBL" href="schedule/2014/spring/GLBL.xml">Global Studies</subject><course id="296" href="schedule/2014/spring/GLBL/296.xml">Global St Foundation Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>B  </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Water Development</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 21-Jan-14 - 14-Mar-14.</sectionDateRange><creditHours>1 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course will explore the complexities of water and access to water in the current global context. Throughout the various sections of the course, materials and discussions will emphasize the differential impact of water scarcity on the global North and global South, the differences of water scarcity processes among countries of the global South, and the ways in which gender impacts policy and access.</sectionText><partOfTerm>A</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2014-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2014-03-14Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>03:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>T      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>G36</roomNumber><buildingName>Foreign Languages Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Kilgore" firstName="J">Kilgore, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>